course: dictionary
lesson: 8025
title: Refocus: bringing your attention back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your attention is like a torch beam. Sometimes it wanders off to something else, and you need to point it back. To refocus means to bring your attention or effort back to something, or onto something new. «Zoning out happens to everyone and is not laziness; you can refocus by asking yourself a question about the topic.» Zoning out means your mind has drifted, and refocus means your mind comes back.
explain: Refocus is also used for cameras, telescopes and eyes. When a picture looks blurry, you adjust the lens again until it is sharp. That is the first meaning in a different setting: the picture was out of focus, and now it is in focus.
explain: You can use the context to check. Ask: does my meaning fit the sentence? In «Let's refocus» said by a teacher, the class is being asked to pay attention again. It does not mean the class should leave the room or stop learning.
fact: Refocus is a verb, so you can say «I refocus», «she refocuses» or «we refocused».
fact: Refocus can also be a noun: «a refocus» is the act of bringing your attention back.
fact: «Refocus» means to bring your attention or effort back to something, or onto something new.
fact: «Refocus» can also mean to adjust a camera, telescope or your eyes again so that the picture becomes sharp.
fact: Both «refocuses» and «refocusses» are accepted spellings, and «refocused» and «refocussed» are too.
exercise: «Zoning out happens to everyone and is not laziness; you can refocus by asking yourself a question about the topic.» What does refocus mean here? | Forget the topic forever | Start a new game | Fall asleep at your desk | *Bring your attention back to the topic
exercise: Your teacher says, «Let's refocus,» when the class gets distracted. What does the teacher want? | Stop the lesson for lunch | *Everyone to bring their attention back to the lesson | Clear the desks | Start a music break
exercise: In science, you refocus a microscope. What do you change so the picture becomes sharp? | The colour of the table | The name of the microscope | The floor | *The lens, until the picture is sharp
test: A coach tells a player to refocus after a mistake. What is the coach asking the player to do? | Go home early | Blame the referee | Run off the pitch | *Put attention back on the game
test: Which word completes the phrase «refocus your ___»? | sandwich | *attention | weather | shoes
exam: In the sentence «Her quick refocus saved the game», what kind of word is refocus? | Adjective | Adverb | Verb | *Noun
